ng_Chin-fang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;\u00eang Chin-fang\">Ch'\u00eang Chin-fang</a></div><div class=\"wst-header-forward-arrow\">\u2192</div></div></div><div class=\"wst-header-notes header&#95;notes searchaux wst-unknown-notes\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14791120\">.mw-parser-output .plainSister{display:block;font-size:93%;line-height:normal;list-style-type:none;list-style-image:none;list-style-position:outside;border:1px solid var(--border-color-interactive--hover,#AAA);float:right;clear:right;margin:0.5ex 0 0.5ex 0.5ex;padding:0;background:var(--background-color-base,#FFFFFF);color:var(--color-base,#202122)}.mw-parser-output .sisicon,.mw-parser-output .dabicon{padding-right:1ex}</style><ul class=\"plainSister\"><li class=\"sisitem\"><span class=\"sisicon\"><span typeof=\"mw:File/Frameless\"><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\"><img alt=\"Sister Projects\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/20px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" width=\"18\" height=\"18\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Wikimedia-logo.svg/40px-Wikimedia-logo.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikisource.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1024\" data-file-height=\"1024\" /></a></span></span><a href=\"/wiki/Special:SiteMatrix\" title=\"Special:SiteMatrix\">sister projects</a>: <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cheng_Jiasui\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"w:Cheng Jiasui\">Wikipedia article</a>, <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q107367067\" class=\"extiw\" title=\"d:Q107367067\">Wikidata item</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"ws-noexport\" id=\"ws-data\" style=\"speak:none\"><span id=\"ws-article-id\">3634138</span><span id=\"ws-title\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period\">Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period</a>, Volume 1 \u2014 Ch&#39;\u00eang Chia-sui</span><span id=\"ws-editor\">Arthur W. Hummel</span><span id=\"ws-author\">J. C. Yang</span></div></div>\n<p><span style=\"display:none\" id=\"dynamic&#95;layout&#95;overrider\">Layout 2</span>\n</p>\n<div class=\"prp-pages-output\" lang=\"en\">\n<p><span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"113\" data-page-number=\"113\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/125\" data-page-index=\"125\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/125\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;125\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span><b>CH'\u00caNG</b> Chia-sui \u7a0b\u5609\u71e7 (<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r14767791\">.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip{cursor:help;border-bottom:thin dotted cornflowerblue}.mw-parser-output .wst-tooltip-nodash{border-bottom:none}</style><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u5b5f\u967d,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u5048\u5eb5, \u677e\u5713\u8a69\u8001), 1565\u20131644, Jan\u2013Feb., Ming poet and painter, was a native of Hsiu-ning, Anhwei, but resided most of his life (about fifty years) in Chia-ting, Kiangsu. Failing to pass the official examinations, he abandoned all hope of a political career and specialized in poetry. When he was about thirty <i>sui</i> he was recognized as an accomplished poet. In 1617 he paid a visit to <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27ien_Ch%27ien-i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;ien Ch&#39;ien-i\">Ch'ien Ch'ien-i</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>] at the latter's villa, Fu-shui Shan-chuang (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Ch%27ien_Ch%27ien-i\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Ch&#39;ien Ch&#39;ien-i\">Ch'ien Ch'ien-i</a></span>), where the two discussed the art of writing poetry, and established a life-long friendship. In the following year he accompanied his friend, Fang Yu-tu \u65b9\u6709\u5ea6 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u65b9\u53d4,&#32;<i>chin-shih</i> of 1616), to Ch'ang-chih, Shansi, when the latter was appointed magistrate of that district. After three years in Ch'ang-chih he proceeded to Peking where he made the acquaintance of Wang Wei-chien \u738b\u7dad\u5109 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u640d\u4ef2,&#32;<i>chin-shih</i> of 1595), whose fame then rivalled that of <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Tung_Ch%27i-ch%27ang\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Tung Ch&#39;i-ch&#39;ang\">Tung Ch'i-ch'ang</a></span>&#32;[<i>q.&#8239;v.</i>]. In 1630 Ch'ien Ch'ien-i again invited Ch'\u00eang to his villa where the two composed a number of poems. While living at Chia-ting, Ch'\u00eang also made a number of friends, notably T'ang Shih-sh\u00eang \u5510\u6642\u5347 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u53d4\u9054,&#32;1551\u20131636) and Lou Chien \u5a41\u5805 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u4e8c\u5805, \u5b50\u67d4,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u6b47\u5eb5,&#32;senior licentiate of 1616, d. 1631). The three came to be known as the \"Three Elders of Lien-ch'uan\" (\u7df4\u5ddd\u4e09\u8001). When Hsieh San-pin \u8b1d\u4e09\u8cd3 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u8c61\u5c71,&#32;<i>chin-shih</i> of 1625) served as&#32;<span><span class=\"pagenum ws-pagenum\" id=\"114\" data-page-number=\"114\" data-page-name=\"Page:Eminent Chinese Of The Ch\u2019ing Period - Hummel - 1943 - Vol. 1.pdf/126\" data-page-index=\"126\" data-page-quality=\"4\" title=\"Page:Eminent&#95;Chinese&#95;Of&#95;The&#95;Ch%E2%80%99ing&#95;Period&#95;-&#95;Hummel&#95;-&#95;1943&#95;-&#95;Vol.&#95;1.pdf/126\"><span id=\"pageindex&#95;126\" class=\"pagenum-inner ws-noexport\">&#8203;</span></span></span>magistrate of Chia-ting he published their poems, together with those of Li Liu-fang \u674e\u6d41\u82b3 (<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Courtesy name (Tz\u00fb/Zi, \u5b57)\">T.</span>&#160;\u9577\u8605, \u8302\u5bb0,&#32;<link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r14767791\" /><span class=\"wst-tooltip wst-tooltip-dash\" title=\"Literary name (Hao, \u865f)\">H.</span>&#160;\u9999\u6d77, \u6ce1\u5eb5, \u614e\u5a1b\u5c45\u58eb), under the collective title \u5609\u5b9a\u56db\u5148\u751f\u96c6 <i>Chia-ting ss\u016d hsien-sh\u00eang chi</i>.\n</p><p>Ch'\u00eang's own poems were published under the title \u677e\u5713\u6d6a\u6dd8\u96c6 <i>Sung-y\u00fcan lang-t'ao chi</i>, in 18 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, with a preface by the author dated 1618. Two other collections by him, entitled \u8026\u8015\u5802\u96c6 <i>Ou-k\u00eang t'ang chi</i>, in 5 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, and \u5048\u5eb5\u96c6 <i>Ch'i-an chi</i>, in 2 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, were banned during the Ch'ing period. Ch'\u00eang also compiled a gazetteer of the Hsing-fu monastery on Mount P'o, Kiangsu, \u7834\u5c71\u8208\u798f\u5bfa\u5fd7 <i>P'o-shan Hsing-fu ss\u016d chih</i>, in 4 <i>ch\u00fcan</i>, which is praised in the <i>Ss\u016d-k'u</i> Catalogue (see under <span class=\"ws-authlkpl\"><a href=\"/wiki/Eminent_Chinese_of_the_Ch%27ing_Period/Chi_Y%C3%BCn\" title=\"Eminent Chinese of the Ch&#39;ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn\">Chi Y\u00fcn</a></span>) for its style. In 1641 he retired to Hsiu-ning and died early in 1644, a few months before the fall of Peking.\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431518\">.mw-parser-output .wst-rule{background-color:currentcolor;color:inherit;width:auto;margin:2px auto 2px auto;height:1px;overflow:hidden}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-left{margin-left:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.wst-rule-right{margin-right:0}.mw-parser-output .wst-rule.__uirule{background-color:#a2a9b1;color:inherit;border:0;margin-top:0.2em;margin-bottom:0.2em}</style><hr class=\"wst-rule wst-rule-left\" style=\"color:inherit;width:40%;\" />\n<p>[M.1/288/7b; M.40/65/7b; M.64/\u5e9a4/1a; M.84/\u4e01\u4e0b/4a; M.86/18/18b; L.T.C.L.H.M., p. 326a; <i>Ss\u016d-k'u</i> \u5730\u7406\u5b58 6; <i>Chia-ting hsien-chih</i> (1882) 13/11a, 20/31b; \u7df4\u5ddd\u540d\u4eba\u756b\u50cf <i>Lien-ch'uan ming-j\u00ean hua-hsiang</i>, \u9644 <i>ch\u00fcan</i> \u4e0b/4a (with portrait).]\n</p>\n<style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r15431519\">.mw-parser-output .wst-right{text-align:right}</style><div class=\"wst-right\" style=\"margin-right:2em;\">\n<p><span class=\"smallcaps\" style=\"font-variant:small-caps;\">J. C. Yang</span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<p><br />\n&#32;\n</p>\n</div>\n</div>"},"links":[{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'ien Ch'ien-i"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch'\u00eang Chin-fang"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Chi Y\u00fcn"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Ch\u00eang, Prince"},{"ns":0,"exists":"","*":"Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period/Tung Ch'i-ch'ang"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:Arthur W. Hummel"},{"ns":102,"exists":"","*":"Author:J. C. Yang"}],"sections":[],"wikitext":{"*":"{{Eminent Chinese of the Ch'ing Period\n | volume   = 1\n | onlysection = ch'eng chia-sui\n | previous = Ch\u00eang, Prince\n | next     = Ch'\u00eang Chin-fang\n | from     = 125\n | to       = 126\n | notes    = \n | section_author = J. C. Yang\n}}{{DEFAULTSORT:Ch'\u00eang Chia-sui}}"}}}